<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.801 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.801 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due March 24, 1997 was 2.801 percent, down from 2.868 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 175-day T-bills due July 17, 1997 was 3.078 percent, down from 3.260 percent last week, and on C$1.2 billion of 364-day T-bills due January 22, 1998 was 3.495 percent, down from 3.713 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$475 million three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$125 million one-year bills. It holds C$925 million of C$6.3 billion of bills due Jan 30. (Details follow)  </p>
